'''''Ferocactus macrodiscus''''' is a [[species]] of [[cactus]] (family Cactaceae) in the [[genus]] [[Ferocactus]] from [[Guanahuato]] and [[Oaxaca]] States,  [[Mexico]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tropicos.org/Name/50004733|title= Ferocactus macrodiscus in Tropicos}}</ref> 
==Description==
It has a globular body about {{convert|4|in|cm}} high and up to {{convert|18|in|cm}} wide,  with typically in maturity 13 to 21 vertical ridges or ribs, based on its adherence to the primary [[Fibonacci]] series. Areoles are  5 to 10 mm long with 1-4 central spines that are 3.5 cm long and 6-8 radial spines that are 2-3 cm long. Spines range from yellow to red, and curved. The plant blooms from early spring to summer. It is most noteworthy for its pink, approx. two inch (5&nbsp;cm) wide  flowers, which have approximately 200 [[tepals]] arranged in a continuous spiral series from perfect sepals on the outside gradually morphing into perfect petals near the center. Fruits are red and spherical 4 x 3 cm with 2 mm long dark brown seeds. <ref>{{cite book |  last1= Britton | first1= Nathan L. | last2= Rose | first2= Joseph E. | date= 1963|edition=reprint| title= The Cactaceae - Volume 3 | location= New York | publisher= Dover Publications | page= Illustration p. 140 }}</ref>
